# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored; never commit real keys.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env.local is read by `make test-local`, `make run` and `make review-pins`.
# The `verify-near-tee` command does NOT read it: export the variables in your
# shell instead (e.g. `set -a; . ./.env.local; set +a`).
#
# Only NEAR_API_KEY_PROD is required for a standard production verification run.
# Everything else has a working default.

# ─── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Bearer token for NEAR's attestation endpoint. Required in every environment.
# Request one from https://cloud.near.ai.
# Keys are per environment; the verifier selects by NEAR_ENV, so set the one
# matching the environment you intend to verify.
NEAR_API_KEY_PROD=
# NEAR_API_KEY_STAGING=
# Fallbacks used for any environment without its own key above.
# NEAR_API_KEY=
# API_KEY=

# ─── Common ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Which NEAR deployment to verify: prod (default) or staging. This also selects
# the audited gateway pins in verifier/config.py.
# NEAR_ENV=prod

# Marketplace model id to verify. One model per run.
# MODEL_NAME=z-ai/glm-5.3-flash

# Gateway base URL. Defaults from NEAR_ENV (prod -> https://cloud-api.near.ai,
# staging -> https://cloud-stg-api.near.ai). Override only to point at a
# different deployment.
# BASE_URL=https://cloud-api.near.ai

# ─── Optional ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# S3 bucket for the report plus the pre-verified/, signing-keys/,
# serving-compose/ and serving-log/ markers.
# Unset means no S3 persistence, which is the normal case for an outside
# verification run. See the README on why the pre-verified/ prefix is part of
# the access gate before pointing this at a shared bucket.
# NEAR_BUCKET_NAME=

# Set (to any non-empty value, even 0) to force full re-verification of every
# image, skipping the pre-verified cache. Use for a clean-room audit run. Slow: provenance plus a
# reproducibility rebuild can take 30 minutes to 2 hours per image.
# PRE_VERIFY_DISABLED=1

# Directory to keep source clones between runs, keyed by image digest. A cached
# clone is used only if its HEAD is the provenance commit, and the image is
# always rebuilt. Only point this at a directory you control.
# BUILD_CACHE_DIR=

# Path to a script that replaces EVERY image's own build script during the
# reproducibility rebuild (e.g. scripts/build-wrapper.sh, a buildx build
# modelled on cloud-api's). Debugging aid only: a match then means "this script reproduces the
# digest", not "the project's own build does".
# BUILD_WRAPPER_SCRIPT=

# Standalone docker-compose binary to use instead of the docker compose plugin.
# It must be the pinned COMPOSE_VERSION in verifier/config.py.
# COMPOSE_BIN=

# ─── Maintainer-only (make review-pins) ────────────────────────────────────────

# Editor diff command; {have}/{need} are substituted with the two commits.
# PIN_REVIEW_DIFF_CMD=nvim -c "DiffviewOpen {have}..{need}"

# Claude CLI used by the [s]can privacy review.
# PIN_REVIEW_CLAUDE_CMD=claude

# Privacy-review prompt for [s]can. Not shipped with the repo; without it
# [s]can declines. Defaults to
# scripts/privacy_review_prompt.md, which is gitignored.
# PIN_REVIEW_PROMPT_FILE=

# Branch the generated pin-bump PR targets.
# PIN_REVIEW_BASE_BRANCH=master

# Override the CodeBuild trigger command; {env} is substituted.
# PIN_REVIEW_CODEBUILD_CMD=

# Brave-internal: the CodeBuild project fired after a pin-bump PR merges, and
# the aws-vault profile allowed to start it. If either is unset (and
# PIN_REVIEW_CODEBUILD_CMD is too), nothing is fired.
# CODEBUILD_PROJECT=
# AWS_VAULT_PROFILE=

# review-pins reads MODEL_NAME (a comma-separated list of model ids) from the
# shell only, not from this file. It defaults to every model pinned in
# config._PROXY_EXPECTED_COMMITS.

# Note: the NVIDIA NRAS URL and the Intel PCCS URL are constants in
# verifier/config.py, not environment variables.
